#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119548 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "244793f6-41c3-5920-9264-bec32cda9c9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4807" :question/problem "The matrix $B$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. \nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(B).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the values of $x_1$ and $x_2,$ where $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{b}_1+x_2\\mathbf{b}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{b}_1,$ $\\mathbf{b}_2$ are the respective columns of $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/assets/b8e5970e24616ddcb86603e266955cc15c7704796eead3f3596ba1f588bb0465.png)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(B),$ we need to check if the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 15 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the true statement $0=0.$ So the system is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=0.$ Substituting into the first equation gives $x_1=\\dfrac 7 5.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(B).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/assets/6e24e4831759f4f4a8b24ec7b3c1c2c7cc44df6be36c5679d2ac8b33a17d8c5c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119549 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "12f222d8-5563-544a-8154-fb1f9406b231" :question/math-academy-id "e-4808" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(C).$ In affirmative case, find the value of $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3$, where $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{c}_1+x_2\\mathbf{c}_3+x_3\\mathbf{c}_3,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/assets/ae098d868e48d331a3cf9f73fe0995eadb60c86e1a74eec039b9044592c55a5c.png)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=1$. Substituting into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+4(1) & =1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-(-1)-4(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/assets/210497f8b94b3600ef3b784333c7388f65678cd18fb7fdd64f9cc14f0b37c87e.png)\n\nFinally, we get $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = 2 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 1 = -2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "b6d52e39-a8a0-5048-80a1-a342a2617e0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6208" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/assets/7565496e57b9dede7d994f9e8ee936e158f67cc8c7397e182c9c6e940939f823.png) Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/assets/b3be9df23c26f562cd1e7c5e1162e87bcc7da0085c00b0185221a6ae45f11395.png) belongs to $\\textrm{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+11{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-4,$ which means that $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "293755df-e490-5555-8d8a-afdd6855ff4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347940} {:answer/id #uuid "9af324b8-8cbb-5b29-856e-9e57613bf50d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347941} {:answer/id #uuid "b36381c9-11c2-562f-a548-e33f55f07675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347942} {:answer/id #uuid "817f7708-e51a-5af2-9155-854aa343303d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347943} {:answer/id #uuid "b6764eb4-019d-5be5-965a-4504248d69fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9af324b8-8cbb-5b29-856e-9e57613bf50d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347941} :answer-field/id #uuid "2377f996-8d5a-5c62-87f0-15e436338522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "950a63de-379e-5572-9290-ed73b2afb97b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110938" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ebef1bb-6358-517d-b973-0e8fd2f5626d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347947} {:answer/id #uuid "691f568c-0984-5d09-8828-192d98da2f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347948} {:answer/id #uuid "afc3d495-f4c9-5ecb-abd4-e085ed025802" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347949} {:answer/id #uuid "6bead015-8a46-510a-9b15-e047bdb21016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347950} {:answer/id #uuid "f3256b8f-6f73-5910-a4ab-b618aae0d403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bead015-8a46-510a-9b15-e047bdb21016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347950} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f8b75ff-968d-5c2f-b1fa-a4169c04ee2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e891c15-a510-513e-8529-e3edc86e4486" :question/math-academy-id "q-110955" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{1},$  ${m}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $M.$ \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=6.$  \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1}$ and ${m}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=6\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=6(-2)=-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "916b6ddf-54fc-5906-95c6-54637926268f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347954} {:answer/id #uuid "66f0094d-849a-5cf1-b4f5-6e903c38433b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347955} {:answer/id #uuid "2a466e31-e1d9-5488-bb74-7515f51075d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347956} {:answer/id #uuid "71025dc0-9d9f-5374-ab67-dce0932d91d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347957} {:answer/id #uuid "f808fa5c-97ab-5f02-9a18-57cb5c80a71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a466e31-e1d9-5488-bb74-7515f51075d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347956} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c925ab3-4264-5f95-bae0-68b87ce13005" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "846d4341-6ad3-5262-9700-ff03087776b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-110969" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 0=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get the false statement $0=12.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(C).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5406bc1-504e-5084-8b55-d08489ff2f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347961} {:answer/id #uuid "b3078e8f-ded9-5a5a-999a-8c52ac449958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347962} {:answer/id #uuid "54c0967f-d02b-5f00-9997-c97829df2731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347963} {:answer/id #uuid "42823540-be03-5133-8a10-83b62141edbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347964} {:answer/id #uuid "396431ce-f36d-5eb7-82ba-736b7d543687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42823540-be03-5133-8a10-83b62141edbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347964} :answer-field/id #uuid "8617977f-b185-5039-9293-160adcda49f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03ae0858-735e-5030-867d-da09e5488318" :question/math-academy-id "q-110976" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $L=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}7k-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $Lx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[L\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 & 7k-1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7k-7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 0=7k-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=7k-7,$ which means that $k=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17a8ff8a-f9ea-510a-bd06-359d1c3adb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347968} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8d18a1-f341-5acb-a211-7bafd4cd28a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347969} {:answer/id #uuid "92735847-d9c0-52a8-9f30-93ff0d882413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347970} {:answer/id #uuid "60c217c9-5977-5441-931b-08e6419c5c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347971} {:answer/id #uuid "7098e457-bd04-5d25-a258-293774162c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7098e457-bd04-5d25-a258-293774162c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347972} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d3f6df4-3412-5177-9e4d-cc7d57e2fa3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c394d631-376c-50ad-ac7b-6e042d3a1f4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-110979" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ k \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=k \\\\ 0=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15809df-e146-591f-8dbb-eac5645accd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347975} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc5bf89-a6ec-5b1c-938d-cb729502d2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347976} {:answer/id #uuid "49c7de10-8ed5-572f-a8b1-4d5c1c3f860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347977} {:answer/id #uuid "fc71caed-f615-5f82-8f1b-12c550a77791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347978} {:answer/id #uuid "68ff4154-32e3-5cd9-a9aa-e7ae34445005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49c7de10-8ed5-572f-a8b1-4d5c1c3f860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347977} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ff9280-01f1-5cac-985a-fa88463bca6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff0bbb5f-ae86-5c12-b1d0-f9a1bb519265" :question/math-academy-id "q-110982" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3},$ and ${c}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}$, and ${c}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-12 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(2) & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-8-3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-8-3(-5)-3(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2=-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1113df2-09e7-5913-b3ac-952e0642cb25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347982} {:answer/id #uuid "289051b8-cdcf-5047-94c5-b91a95940131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347983} {:answer/id #uuid "80d5a912-c8ae-52d3-b4c2-6d231899e6b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347984} {:answer/id #uuid "56eebeab-ca6b-5656-a522-d45e5270b54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347985} {:answer/id #uuid "c6dd5f54-bd21-51f1-9158-3077ccf12668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "289051b8-cdcf-5047-94c5-b91a95940131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347983} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee25df5c-4bc0-5be0-97c5-9a3ed026715c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da97535f-d1dd-5002-bedc-964f546b7a57" :question/math-academy-id "q-110983" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, and ${m}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -24 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ {x}_{2}=8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+(8) & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1},$ ${m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+8\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot 8\\cdot 2=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bcd104f-821a-5cec-a110-f47fa514baef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347989} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4a3827-ab29-5230-8a3e-c35fe6c09dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347990} {:answer/id #uuid "64d3d256-21e4-589c-8b81-b7619ea3733c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347991} {:answer/id #uuid "01a6de09-7514-53a7-8c88-edde72d0ec00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347992} {:answer/id #uuid "3380021f-a211-5df1-aa84-4d04bd2c3b9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c4a3827-ab29-5230-8a3e-c35fe6c09dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347990} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbbecf90-a67f-58cc-a44d-1e808a1f885d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347988}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cff46c9b-f103-5ae7-b9ea-0cb79478d7b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-111053" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3}+{x}_{4}{m}_{4},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, ${m}_{3}$, and ${m}_{4}$ are respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}+4{x}_{4}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=1 \\\\ 0=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=8.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(M).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cfc203-72c3-5bfa-a5ee-fa85fc2280bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347996} {:answer/id #uuid "29dd1a1c-abb4-5e71-ad06-9ce09957e710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347997} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfbb5f0-e7ba-5857-8e9e-62771555de5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347998} {:answer/id #uuid "c9264877-5cad-5494-bc40-9ad497e79fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347999} {:answer/id #uuid "386b6587-327f-5158-83be-c7477bf9581e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "386b6587-327f-5158-83be-c7477bf9581e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348000} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba4d6b9-559b-50d7-915f-631794b30c6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9e5d37f-5b0d-54e5-8ca2-d4aa4f3fb560" :question/math-academy-id "q-34346" :question/problem "The matrix $D$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}+7{x}_{4}=11 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=-2 \\\\ 0=9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "951868fd-9ced-5f7b-be6d-e7f8b082b2df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348003} {:answer/id #uuid "dddebe88-1b25-50e0-ae4b-a05461742c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348004} {:answer/id #uuid "84c167ff-4894-5ee6-8b72-cb4d6fe65ef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348005} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b39a6b-63f2-59f0-8ec3-4c3ee0f38842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348006} {:answer/id #uuid "c306cdb7-9cb1-5cc9-a268-2aca4ad58454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "951868fd-9ced-5f7b-be6d-e7f8b082b2df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348003} :answer-field/id #uuid "6350e8ca-f173-5f16-9f62-0aec79b7cc20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ec951e45-40b8-5089-a489-6b4ed8a26d7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34364" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=4 \\\\ 0=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff8b0fbb-de51-53e8-b662-51cb61e8351e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348010} {:answer/id #uuid "e4143b2f-72bf-5fa1-9252-a0d13be22642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348011} {:answer/id #uuid "83f3449c-660e-5002-8a1c-5a3f6249a7a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348012} {:answer/id #uuid "c1197d82-089b-5230-92e6-e73ff4ab7dca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348013} {:answer/id #uuid "44d1817d-dbdf-510d-b141-5153a42a74ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44d1817d-dbdf-510d-b141-5153a42a74ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348014} :answer-field/id #uuid "46130ca7-8d93-5012-bdd9-99b7669258b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afd8a578-b320-5dea-80a5-576663587d89" :question/math-academy-id "q-34366" :question/problem "The matrix $F$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{f}_{1}+{x}_{2}{f}_{2},$ and ${f}_{1},$  ${f}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $F.$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(F),$ we need to check if the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[F\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[F\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=1.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=1\\cdot (-2)=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40089017-e63f-5e8d-b8b6-334d9f4683d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348017} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5565a3-6675-550f-87a2-1cc2bd719d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348018} {:answer/id #uuid "932925fd-7c14-5620-a48d-f5fe93bdb03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348019} {:answer/id #uuid "ed41b598-651d-5a77-a671-f6ec4835afbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348020} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ef32d3-2b6d-58ff-8d2c-450af8f069b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40089017-e63f-5e8d-b8b6-334d9f4683d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348017} :answer-field/id #uuid "54ee1695-9368-518e-8757-0e245b84d3f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f650b056-4330-5cfb-8710-f9d6cae65222" :question/math-academy-id "q-35562" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 17 & k-12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-17){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=k+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+5,$ which means that $k=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b830469-2ecc-55d3-87e1-b065cbb31f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348024} {:answer/id #uuid "c832bf8c-7c32-5b15-9e76-8b9a450f8355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348025} {:answer/id #uuid "a0979af1-89e2-557c-9e5d-1ba466667e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348026} {:answer/id #uuid "52bc3d02-be48-578e-a3fe-16166c661bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348027} {:answer/id #uuid "43b38a66-f23e-57f3-a5f2-96a8661900f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0979af1-89e2-557c-9e5d-1ba466667e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348026} :answer-field/id #uuid "41e9676d-8de4-5d90-848b-7b781480fe38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6fba4bd1-d9b0-5ca0-a111-f15a2d569cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74198" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a944fe9-8dd8-58bd-84f6-1c018ff9d638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348031} {:answer/id #uuid "0e71ca9b-4fda-5265-8302-45ab19231a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348032} {:answer/id #uuid "2a07ac49-8931-52b4-b2bb-c6b972a0215c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348033} {:answer/id #uuid "2cae8249-7514-5de5-bc2f-9ab4e1c78d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348034} {:answer/id #uuid "06ee4f34-5c68-5f71-bbaf-60b937266241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e71ca9b-4fda-5265-8302-45ab19231a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348032} :answer-field/id #uuid "50b2b13e-677b-5e86-872d-0b5adddcee92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2f3a0be-8c3d-5660-a230-2fc5e874764e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74209" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k-3\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(B).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(B),$ then the equation $Bx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k+2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=k-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-1,$ which means that $k=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22abf599-5b3b-5bb1-93b1-6eb66a2b2c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348038} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c9c193-91d2-54b9-8e39-9e30cddb1ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348039} {:answer/id #uuid "c71a99ff-38dc-5098-8d04-332170d5db90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348040} {:answer/id #uuid "3574ab7e-a81f-5693-b5ea-3c1e9a81f33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348041} {:answer/id #uuid "e0082990-b9f1-5bf4-8c64-434af0e38c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0082990-b9f1-5bf4-8c64-434af0e38c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348042} :answer-field/id #uuid "07681964-3a1d-53ca-850a-73d053489805" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2221f0e-e99c-52d9-8edc-8f3c3f403a96" :question/math-academy-id "q-74213" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $M=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2k+10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(M).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ then the equation $Mx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 15 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=2k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=2k-10,$ which means that $k=5.$"}]}
